"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_010_thumb.jpg", "page": "14", "label": "10", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/14"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_011_thumb.jpg", "page": "15", "label": "11", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/15"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_012_thumb.jpg", "page": "16", "label": "12", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/16"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_013_thumb.jpg", "page": "17", "label": "13", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/17"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_014_thumb.jpg", "page": "18", "label": "14", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/18"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_015_thumb.jpg", "page": "19", "label": "15", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/19"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_016_thumb.jpg", "page": "20", "label": "16", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/20"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_017_thumb.jpg", "page": "21", "label": "17", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/21"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_018_thumb.jpg", "page": "22", "label": "18", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/22"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_019_thumb.jpg", "page": "23", "label": "[19]", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/23"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_020_thumb.jpg", "page": "24", "label": "[20]", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/24"}], "tableOfContents": [], "summary": {"uri": "ordinance-14-november-1842", "series": "JSPPA", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPA6", "documentSeriesIdCompiled": "jsppa6-sub-nccr-sub02-421114", "documentSeriesUri": "/the-papers/administrative-records/jsppa6/jsppa6-sub-nccr/jsppa6-sub-nccr-sub02/jsppa6-sub-nccr-sub02-421114", "documentSeriesTitle": "<p>\r\n\tMeeting, 14 November 1842</p>", "editorialPageNumber": "8", "isPageNumberPresent": true, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/54016763/54016763-0012.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> may have been executed by a Person or Persons not duly authorized, the Court shall make a new Commitment, in proper form, and directed to the proper officer or officers, or admit the party to bail, if the Case be bailable.</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\">Sec. 4. When any person or Persons shall be admitted to Bail, on <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"17916630642311328082\"><a href=\"#17916630642311328082\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x41899\" topic=\"x41899\" title=\"Habeas corpus\">Habeas Corpus</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Habeas corpus\"><p>“Have the body”; a written order from a court of competent jurisdiction commanding anyone having a person in custody to produce such person at a certain time and place and to state the reasons why he or she is being held in custody. The court will determine...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/habeas-corpus\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside>, he she or they shall enter into <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"9993179997109010040\"><a href=\"#9993179997109010040\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x33313\" topic=\"x33313\" title=\"Recognizance\">Recognizance</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Recognizance\"><p>“An obligation of record . . . to do some act required by law,” such as “to keep the peace, to pay a debt, or the like.” Recognizance is “somewhat like an ordinary bond, the difference being that a bond is the creation of a fresh debt, or obligation de novo...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/recognizance\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> with one or more securities in such sum as the Court shall direct, having regard to the circumstances of the Prisoner or Prisoners, and the nature of the offence, conditioned for his her or their appearance at the next Circuit Court, to be holden in and for the County where the offence was committed, or where the same is to be tried: Where the Court shall admit to Bail, or remand any Prisoner or Prisoners brought before the Court, on any Writ of Habeas Corpus, it shall be the duty of said Court to bind all such Persons as do declare any thing material to prove the offence with which the Prisoner or Prisoners are charged, by Recognizance, to appear at the proper Court [p. 8]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> may have been executed by a Person &lt;​or Persons​&gt; not duly authorized, <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>the Court shall make a new Commitment, in proper <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>form, and directed to the proper officer &lt;​or officers​&gt;, or admit the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>party to bail, if the Case be bailable.</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\">Sec. 4. When any person &lt;​or Persons​&gt; shall be admitted to Bail, on <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"14030143299849232826\"><a href=\"#14030143299849232826\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x41899\" topic=\"x41899\" title=\"Habeas corpus\">Habeas Corpus</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Habeas corpus\"><p>“Have the body”; a written order from a court of competent jurisdiction commanding anyone having a person in custody to produce such person at a certain time and place and to state the reasons why he or she is being held in custody. The court will determine...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/habeas-corpus\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside>, he &lt;​she or they​&gt; shall enter into <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"2748101125309080347\"><a href=\"#2748101125309080347\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x33313\" topic=\"x33313\" title=\"Recognizance\">Recognizance</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Recognizance\"><p>“An obligation of record . . . to do some act required by law,” such as “to keep the peace, to pay a debt, or the like.” Recognizance is “somewhat like an ordinary bond, the difference being that a bond is the creation of a fresh debt, or obligation de novo...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/recognizance\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>with one or more securities in such sum as the Court <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>shall direct, having regard to the circumstances of the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>Prisoner &lt;​or Prisoners​&gt;, and the nature of the offence, conditioned for his <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>&lt;​her​&gt; or <span class=\"deleted\">her</span> &lt;​their​&gt; appearance at the next Circuit Court, to be holden <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>in and for the County where the offence was committed, <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>or where the same is to be tried: Where the Court shall <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>admit to Bail, or remand any Prisoner &lt;​or Prisoners​&gt; brought before <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>the Court, on any Writ of Habeas Corpus, it shall be the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>duty of said Court to bind all such Persons as do declare <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>any thing material to prove the offence with which the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>Prisoner &lt;​or Prisoners​&gt; <span class=\"deleted\">is</span> &lt;​are​&gt; charged, by Recognizance, to appear at the proper Court [p. 8]</div></body></html>", "calendarsOfDocuments": [], "versions": [{"versionTitle": "Ordinance, 14 November 1842", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/1", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": "Nauvoo City Council Minute Book, 1841–1845", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/nauvoo-city-council-minute-book-1841-1845/125", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": "Ordinance, 14 November 1842, as Published in the <em xmlns:tei=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" xmlns:lds=\"https://ldsc.xmlref.com/local/ldschurch\">Wasp</em>", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842-as-published-in-the-wasp/1", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": "History, 1838–1856, volume D-1 [1 August 1842–1 July 1843]", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/history-1838-1856-volume-d-1-1-august-1842-1-july-1843/58", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": "“History of Joseph Smith”", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/history-of-joseph-smith/451", "versionFeatured": ""}], "images": {"smallImageUrl": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_008_thumb.jpg", "mediumImageUrl": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_008_med.jpg", "largeImageUrl": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_008.jpg", "downloadImageUrl": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_008_download.jpg"}, "imageCredit": "", "facsimile": "", "dzUrlXml": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_008.xml", "classification": "Administrative", "publishedStatus": "FinalContent", "accessionNumber": "11909", "requestedPageNumber": "12", "numberOfPages": "24", "editorialTitle": "Ordinance, 14 November 1842", "cleanEditorialTitle": "Ordinance, 14 November 1842", "date": "November 14, 1842", "handwriting": "Handwriting of James Sloan, two unidentified scribes, and JS", "footnotes": [